[{"label":"Figures that load well","html":"<article class=\"paper typeset-numbered\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span class=\"badge\" data-variant=\"secondary\">Short paper</span\n      ><span>defuss-shadcn · <time datetime=\"2026-10\">October 2026</time></span></p\n    >\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"pm-title\"\n      >Figures That Load Well<span class=\"paper-title-sub\">Images, galleries and video in a paper</span></h1\n    >\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li\n      ><li>Claude</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"pm-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >A figure in a paper should load lazily, keep its space while it loads, fail visibly and open larger on demand; a\n      video should carry captions and chapters. Each of these is a native element with a few attributes. This paper uses\n      three placeholder images - one scene in a neutral, a cool and a warm tone - and a six-second captioned clip.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <nav class=\"paper-toc\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-toc\">\n    <h2 id=\"pm-toc\">Contents</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pm-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>Figures</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pm-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>A series</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pm-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>A clip</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pm-cite\"><span class=\"paper-num\">·&nbsp;</span>Citation and references</a></li\n      >\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-s1\">\n    <h2 id=\"pm-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>Figures</h2>\n    <p\n      >Three versions of one placeholder scene, set densely in one box - each part lettered, the group numbered as one\n      figure:</p\n    >\n    <figure class=\"typeset-group paper-wide\">\n      <figure class=\"image\" data-preview data-ratio=\"16/9\">\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide.png\" alt=\"Placeholder scene, neutral grey: a mountain and a sun\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        <figcaption class=\"typeset-subcaption\">Neutral.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <figure class=\"image\" data-preview data-ratio=\"16/9\">\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide2.png\" alt=\"Placeholder scene, cool blue-grey: a mountain and a sun\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        <figcaption class=\"typeset-subcaption\">Cool.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <figure class=\"image\" data-preview data-ratio=\"16/9\">\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide3.png\" alt=\"Placeholder scene, warm sand: a mountain and a sun\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        <figcaption class=\"typeset-subcaption\">Warm.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <figcaption class=\"typeset-caption\"\n        >One scene in a neutral, a cool and a warm tone; click a picture to open it larger.</figcaption\n      >\n    </figure>\n    <p\n      >Each figure reserves its 16:9 box before the image arrives (<code>data-ratio</code>), so the column never jumps,\n      and opens in a native dialog on click.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-s2\">\n    <h2 id=\"pm-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>A series</h2>\n    <figure>\n      <figure class=\"hover-gallery\" style=\"max-width: 28rem; margin: 0 auto\">\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide.png\" alt=\"The scene in neutral grey\" />\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide2.png\" alt=\"The scene in cool blue-grey\" />\n        <img src=\"images/mk-wide3.png\" alt=\"The scene in warm sand\" />\n        <img src=\"images/mk-square.png\" alt=\"The scene cropped square\" />\n      </figure>\n      <figcaption class=\"typeset-caption\" data-align=\"center\"\n        >Four pictures in one frame: move the pointer across it.</figcaption\n      >\n    </figure>\n    <p\n      >A hover gallery shows a series in one frame: the pointer's position picks the image, and every image is decoded\n      before the first switch, so nothing flashes.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-s3\">\n    <h2 id=\"pm-s3\"><span class=\"paper-num\">3&nbsp;</span>A clip</h2>\n    <figure>\n      <video\n        controls\n        preload=\"metadata\"\n        playsinline\n        poster=\"images/mk-wide3.png\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: var(--radius-lg)\"\n      >\n        <source src=\"videos/demo.webm\" type=\"video/webm\" />\n        <source src=\"videos/demo.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\" />\n        <track kind=\"captions\" src=\"videos/demo.en.vtt\" srclang=\"en\" label=\"English\" default />\n        Your browser does not support video. <a href=\"videos/demo.mp4\">Download the clip</a>.\n      </video>\n      <figcaption class=\"typeset-caption\" data-align=\"justify\"\n        >The demonstration clip of the docs: three captioned scenes of two seconds each - planning the week, linking\n        drafts and tasks, shipping. A justified caption sets its longer lines flush on both sides.</figcaption\n      >\n    </figure>\n    <p\n      >The clip carries a captions track, on by default; its caption continues the paper's figure count, because a video\n      is a figure like a picture or a chart.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"paper-bibtex\" aria-labelledby=\"pm-cite\">\n    <h2 id=\"pm-cite\">Citation and references</h2>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"bibtex apa mla ieee\" aria-label=\"Cite this paper\">\n      <figcaption>Cite this paper</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{homberg2026figures,\n  title = {Figures That Load Well: Images, Galleries and Video in a Paper},\n  author = {Homberg, Aron and Claude},\n  institution = {defuss},\n  year = {2026},\n  month = oct,\n  url = {https://shadcn.defuss.org/papers/paper-media.html}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"ieee apa bibtex\" data-format=\"ieee\" aria-label=\"References\">\n      <figcaption>References</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@misc{whatwg_html,\n  author = {{WHATWG}},\n  title = {HTML Living Standard},\n  url = {https://html.spec.whatwg.org/}\n}\n\n@misc{w3c_webvtt,\n  author = {{W3C}},\n  title = {WebVTT: The Web Video Text Tracks Format},\n  url = {https://www.w3.org/TR/webvtt1/}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026defussshadcn,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {defuss-shadcn: shadcn-style components as semantic HTML},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {GitHub},\n  url = {https://github.com/kyr0/defuss-shadcn}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
